01:15:37.523 --> 01:15:38.893
But like cheese, no way.

01:15:38.893 --> 01:15:39.866
Get that shit out of here.

01:15:39.866 --> 01:15:40.699
We don't need cheese.

01:15:40.699 --> 01:15:43.287
- You know it's fucked when we
have more variations of natto

01:15:43.287 --> 01:15:44.120
than we do cheese.

01:15:44.120 --> 01:15:45.605
(guys laughing)

01:15:45.605 --> 01:15:47.425
I mean, not that I'm
complaining, but yeah.

01:15:47.425 --> 01:15:49.277
- I don't know how you handle natto, man.

01:15:49.277 --> 01:15:51.066
- I just grew up with it, man.

01:15:51.066 --> 01:15:53.696
- I'm open to things.
- Yeah.

01:15:53.696 --> 01:15:56.227
- I think I have a really good palate.

01:15:56.227 --> 01:15:57.924
I can eat anything but natto,

01:15:57.924 --> 01:15:59.148
I don't know what the fuck that is.

01:15:59.148 --> 01:16:01.174
- I don't want to be that guy,
but it's an acquired taste.

01:16:01.174 --> 01:16:02.081
(guys laughing)

01:16:02.081 --> 01:16:02.921
- You can say that again.

01:16:02.921 --> 01:16:05.110
You know, I feel that
I'm pretty international

01:16:05.110 --> 01:16:06.908
and I'm open to try new things.

01:16:06.908 --> 01:16:09.734
There's a few things in the
world that I just don't get.

01:16:09.734 --> 01:16:11.174
Natto is one of them.

01:16:11.174 --> 01:16:13.162
I'm sorry to betray my own country.

01:16:13.162 --> 01:16:14.585
Durian is another one.

01:16:14.585 --> 01:16:15.952
I'm sorry, guys.

01:16:15.952 --> 01:16:16.894
- I've never tried real durian.

01:16:16.894 --> 01:16:18.263
- I've never tried durian as well.

01:16:18.263 --> 01:16:20.492
- But I've always wanted to.

01:16:20.492 --> 01:16:21.788
- What are some like,

01:16:21.788 --> 01:16:22.770
I guess while we're talking about it,

01:16:22.770 --> 01:16:24.801
what are some misconceptions about Japan

01:16:24.801 --> 01:16:26.162
that you think you experienced?

01:16:26.162 --> 01:16:28.889
'Cause for me, I know, I
thought for some reason

01:16:28.889 --> 01:16:30.876
I thought I was gonna eat way more fish

01:16:30.876 --> 01:16:33.057
by just being, I mean, in comparison

01:16:33.057 --> 01:16:35.026
I guess I do eat slightly more fish

01:16:35.026 --> 01:16:37.117
but I thought fish was gonna be way more

01:16:37.117 --> 01:16:39.428
of a factor in my life
than it actually is.

01:16:39.428 --> 01:16:42.670
I feel like if you want
to avoid fish in Japan,

01:16:42.670 --> 01:16:43.677
it is so easy.

01:16:43.677 --> 01:16:45.285
- Oh yeah, very, very.

01:16:45.285 --> 01:16:47.984
I mean, I think that also
comes from the whole fact

01:16:47.984 --> 01:16:49.951
that because there were
more foreigners living here,

01:16:49.951 --> 01:16:51.439
like there were just like,

01:16:51.439 --> 01:16:53.472
especially between the four years

01:16:53.472 --> 01:16:54.855
that I've been living here,

01:16:54.855 --> 01:16:58.121
there are so many more vegetarian
and vegan places open now.

01:16:58.121 --> 01:17:00.751
It's incredible, especially in Tokyo,

01:17:00.751 --> 01:17:02.652
but like, yeah, no, I agree.

01:17:02.652 --> 01:17:04.909
I love me my fish don't get me wrong.

01:17:04.909 --> 01:17:05.742
- Same, same.

01:17:05.742 --> 01:17:08.514
- But I'm definitely not
going to eat sushi every week

01:17:08.514 --> 01:17:10.302
like most my fans think I am.

01:17:10.302 --> 01:17:11.902
- Yeah, I can't eat sushi every day.

01:17:11.902 --> 01:17:13.960
It's like a nice little treat.

01:17:13.960 --> 01:17:14.949
- Right, right.

01:17:14.949 --> 01:17:16.086
- I don't know what you guys are on about.

01:17:16.086 --> 01:17:17.280
If I could eat sushi every week,

01:17:17.280 --> 01:17:20.340
I would and I do most weeks.

01:17:20.340 --> 01:17:21.590
Pre-quarantine,

01:17:22.748 --> 01:17:25.070
going to this dollar sushi chain,

01:17:25.070 --> 01:17:27.679
I fucking love it because
you get better sushi

01:17:27.679 --> 01:17:30.081
than you do for paying 30 quid
or whatever you do in the UK.

01:17:30.081 --> 01:17:32.769
- Oh yeah.
- For a fucking dollar.

01:17:32.769 --> 01:17:34.388
And it's fucking amazing

01:17:34.388 --> 01:17:36.539
and I do eat quite a lot fish

01:17:36.539 --> 01:17:37.999
mostly because I eat sushi a lot

01:17:37.999 --> 01:17:41.122
and when you cook at home,
you know cooking salmon.

01:17:41.122 --> 01:17:42.522
- Oh yeah, I love cooking salmon, cod

01:17:42.522 --> 01:17:43.939
like that's so good.
- Yeah, yah.

01:17:43.939 --> 01:17:46.368
- And because there's so
much fish, like in the UK

01:17:46.368 --> 01:17:47.965
sometimes you could get like meat

01:17:47.965 --> 01:17:50.224
that's been like seasoned already.

01:17:50.224 --> 01:17:52.293
And you can get like fish
and supermarkets here

01:17:52.293 --> 01:17:54.412
that's already been
pre-seasoned, everything,

01:17:54.412 --> 01:17:56.652
so literally all you gotta
do is open that bad boy up,

01:17:56.652 --> 01:17:59.186
throw it in a pan and you've
got an amazing tasting fish.

01:17:59.186 --> 01:18:00.183
It's so good.
- Yeah.

01:18:00.183 --> 01:18:01.654
- I think it's just habit basically,

01:18:01.654 --> 01:18:03.403
because if you don't have
the habit of eating fish,

01:18:03.403 --> 01:18:06.107
there's so many other
shit that you could eat

01:18:06.107 --> 01:18:08.957
because it's so readily available.

01:18:08.957 --> 01:18:10.131
- Pizza potato, that's the best.

01:18:10.131 --> 01:18:11.101
(guys laughing)

01:18:11.101 --> 01:18:12.283
if you don't know what pizza potato is,

01:18:12.283 --> 01:18:13.116
come to the Japan, it's amazing.

01:18:13.116 --> 01:18:16.125
I fucking stand by it.
- But that's the thing right-

01:18:16.125 --> 01:18:18.203
- Sorry, I interrupted you.

01:18:18.203 --> 01:18:21.399
- I think most people think that like, oh,

01:18:21.399 --> 01:18:24.705
all there is to eat is just
like sushi is because like

01:18:24.705 --> 01:18:26.757
as obvious as this is gonna sound,

01:18:26.757 --> 01:18:29.961
Japanese food culture is
just so much more than that.

01:18:29.961 --> 01:18:31.915
It is so much more than fish.

01:18:31.915 --> 01:18:35.735
- I have consistently had
the best Italian food here

01:18:35.735 --> 01:18:37.267
as opposed to-
(Joey laughing)

01:18:37.267 --> 01:18:39.666
- There's someone Italian
out there just cringing.

01:18:39.666 --> 01:18:41.665
- Yeah, he's like what the fuck.

01:18:41.665 --> 01:18:44.237
- Going to Italy, it's no contest, right?

01:18:44.237 --> 01:18:47.075
But compared to the UK where
it was literally like again,

01:18:47.075 --> 01:18:48.030
it was a coin toss, right?

01:18:48.030 --> 01:18:51.053
You'd go to a place and the
pasta was like god awful.

01:18:51.053 --> 01:18:53.514
Like it's the saddest
carbonara, which you know,

01:18:53.514 --> 01:18:54.730
how can you fuck that up?

01:18:54.730 --> 01:18:56.582
That's like pasta 101, right?

01:18:56.582 --> 01:18:58.820
You come here and I feel
like you just always

01:18:58.820 --> 01:19:01.940
consistently have a good
experience with every kind of food.

01:19:01.940 --> 01:19:03.139
Right?
- Right.

01:19:03.139 --> 01:19:06.189
- I mean, you know this, Chinese
food in the UK is a joke.

01:19:06.189 --> 01:19:07.700
- We're not gonna get into that.

01:19:07.700 --> 01:19:08.624
(guys laughing)

01:19:08.624 --> 01:19:10.435
I could spend a lot
talking about Chinese food-

01:19:10.435 --> 01:19:11.856
- Any kind of cuisine you can imagine,

01:19:11.856 --> 01:19:15.360
except maybe like American
food like portion heavy-

01:19:15.360 --> 01:19:16.521
- Like diner food.

01:19:16.521 --> 01:19:19.599
- Yeah meat, like really ribs and stuff.

01:19:19.599 --> 01:19:21.681
Yeah, it's hard to get that,

01:19:21.681 --> 01:19:24.936
but I'm fine with going to
America or going back to the UK

01:19:24.936 --> 01:19:26.936
and having that myself every now and then

01:19:26.936 --> 01:19:29.006
for the overall trade-off of all right,

01:19:29.006 --> 01:19:31.312
consistently I get better meals, right?

01:19:31.312 --> 01:19:32.453
- Right, right, right.

01:19:32.453 --> 01:19:35.013
- Is there anything else that
haven't met your expectations

01:19:35.013 --> 01:19:37.213
or haven't met your preconceptions?

01:19:37.213 --> 01:19:40.475
- I want to know as like
a non-resident, right?

01:19:40.475 --> 01:19:41.846
Or like non-Japanese.

01:19:41.846 --> 01:19:43.612
- This is gonna sound
dumb as fuck, all right?

01:19:43.612 --> 01:19:45.073
And I know it's going to sound dumb,

01:19:45.073 --> 01:19:48.933
but I knew things were
going to be difficult

01:19:48.933 --> 01:19:51.162
that I couldn't speak
Japanese or read Japanese.

01:19:51.162 --> 01:19:52.686
More so read than anything.

01:19:52.686 --> 01:19:55.410
I feel like for some
reason you can be fine

01:19:55.410 --> 01:19:58.009
not speaking Japanese
here, but if you can't read

01:19:58.009 --> 01:20:01.040
like you're in for a storm of trouble

01:20:01.040 --> 01:20:02.823
because there are so many things,

01:20:02.823 --> 01:20:05.032
and I think we all can agree on this.

01:20:05.032 --> 01:20:06.352
If Amazon didn't exist here and-

01:20:06.352 --> 01:20:07.943
- Oh my God.

01:20:07.943 --> 01:20:09.780
- If Amazon didn't have
English settings here,

01:20:09.780 --> 01:20:11.661
I genuinely don't know what I would do

01:20:11.661 --> 01:20:14.111
because the websites here in Japanese,

01:20:14.111 --> 01:20:17.028
like I don't know if
they've done this on purpose

01:20:17.028 --> 01:20:18.781
or due to the old interface,

01:20:18.781 --> 01:20:20.500
they do not work well
with Google Translate.

01:20:20.500 --> 01:20:22.704
- I mean, it's all going
back to that 90s web-

01:20:22.704 --> 01:20:24.536
- No, they don't know how
to design their websites.

01:20:24.536 --> 01:20:25.637
It's not user-friendly.

01:20:25.637 --> 01:20:27.935
So if you can't speak
Japanese or read Japanese

01:20:27.935 --> 01:20:29.520
you're kind of fucked.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:20:29.520 --> 01:20:31.251
And Google Translate does not help.

01:20:31.251 --> 01:20:32.128
- No, it doesn't help.

01:20:32.128 --> 01:20:35.120
It can help you kind of
feel your way through

01:20:35.120 --> 01:20:37.979
but you cannot tell what
the fuck you're doing.

01:20:37.979 --> 01:20:40.106
The only reason we've been
able to get through it

01:20:40.106 --> 01:20:42.096
is because we've had a fucking-

01:20:42.096 --> 01:20:43.903
- Got friends, we got
a company helping us.

01:20:43.903 --> 01:20:45.828
It makes it so much easier.

01:20:45.828 --> 01:20:47.157
Oh yeah, Joey, shout out to Joey.

01:20:47.157 --> 01:20:48.323
- I am that friend.
- Yeah.

01:20:48.323 --> 01:20:50.899
- Joey helped me a lot when we moved here,

01:20:50.899 --> 01:20:52.771
like helped me out doing all the dumb-

01:20:52.771 --> 01:20:53.962
- I had to go to the town hall with you

01:20:53.962 --> 01:20:55.829
to fill our your papers.

01:20:55.829 --> 01:20:57.160
- That's the thing, right?

01:20:57.160 --> 01:21:00.271
It's like you think like
in the big population areas

01:21:00.271 --> 01:21:01.664
they'd have like a lot of English support,

01:21:01.664 --> 01:21:05.044
but I think they said if you
come on these certain days,

01:21:05.044 --> 01:21:06.318
like setting up internet,

01:21:06.318 --> 01:21:07.650
do you remember how much
of a hassle that was?

01:21:07.650 --> 01:21:08.483
- Oh my god.

01:21:08.483 --> 01:21:10.733
- I remember the AU, right?

01:21:11.750 --> 01:21:14.235
They say they have an
English location in Shinjuku.

01:21:14.235 --> 01:21:15.886
- Oh yeah.
- That's a fucking lie.

01:21:15.886 --> 01:21:20.231
- No, no, their English location
is that they have a tablet

01:21:20.231 --> 01:21:22.492
which can call a call center

01:21:22.492 --> 01:21:25.284
that can translate the
person for you kind of,

01:21:25.284 --> 01:21:26.821
but not really but that's the closest-

01:21:26.821 --> 01:21:27.895
- But did you even get that far?

01:21:27.895 --> 01:21:29.606
'Cause I didn't even get
to the guy on the tablet.

01:21:29.606 --> 01:21:31.576
I just turned up saying on the website,

01:21:31.576 --> 01:21:33.530
this says this is the English location.

01:21:33.530 --> 01:21:34.739
And they were like, no.

01:21:34.739 --> 01:21:36.171
And I'm like, well, what do I do?

01:21:36.171 --> 01:21:37.652
How the fuck do I get internet now?

01:21:37.652 --> 01:21:38.485
Help me!

01:21:39.399 --> 01:21:42.426
- Luckily I had a cousin
who worked in Japan

01:21:42.426 --> 01:21:43.453
so she could speak Japanese.

01:21:43.453 --> 01:21:45.058
She helped me through so much

01:21:45.058 --> 01:21:47.947
and I don't know what
I would do without her.

01:21:47.947 --> 01:21:49.878
And same with you.
- Yeah, same, same.

01:21:49.878 --> 01:21:51.184
I need a lot of help.

01:21:51.184 --> 01:21:53.040
- You feel like a baby.

01:21:53.040 --> 01:21:56.208
- I genuinely don't know how,

01:21:56.208 --> 01:21:57.697
there are some foreigners here

01:21:57.697 --> 01:21:59.441
who can't even speak English

01:21:59.441 --> 01:22:02.309
who somehow made it here on their own.

01:22:02.309 --> 01:22:04.787
And I'm like, how the
fuck did you do that?

01:22:04.787 --> 01:22:06.777
- Because at least they have
a lot of English words, right?

01:22:06.777 --> 01:22:09.382
And a lot of English options sometimes

01:22:09.382 --> 01:22:12.505
but if can't speak English,
fuck, I don't know what you-

01:22:12.505 --> 01:22:13.338
- I don't know how they do it.

01:22:13.338 --> 01:22:15.319
- I don't know, like English
is hard enough as it is.

01:22:15.319 --> 01:22:17.225
If you can't speak Japanese

01:22:17.225 --> 01:22:19.399
then I think you're pretty much fucked.

01:22:19.399 --> 01:22:21.289
(guys laughing)

01:22:21.289 --> 01:22:23.372
- Real positive message
coming out of this episode.

01:22:23.372 --> 01:22:25.304
- No, no, no, because that's the thing,

01:22:25.304 --> 01:22:26.694
a lot of people don't talk about

01:22:26.694 --> 01:22:29.437
which is how hard it is to live here,

01:22:29.437 --> 01:22:32.836
actually live here
without speaking Japanese

01:22:32.836 --> 01:22:35.444
because coming on, like
we said, it's so different

01:22:35.444 --> 01:22:38.473
living here as working here

01:22:38.473 --> 01:22:40.624
and just live visiting here as a tourist.

01:22:40.624 --> 01:22:42.864
There's a world of difference.

01:22:42.864 --> 01:22:45.985
And there's so many little
things like for example,

01:22:45.985 --> 01:22:47.445
registering with the town hall.

01:22:47.445 --> 01:22:49.044
How the fuck am I supposed to do that

01:22:49.044 --> 01:22:50.095
if I don't speak Japanese?

01:22:50.095 --> 01:22:52.068
'Cause they don't speak English.

01:22:52.068 --> 01:22:53.549
And all the forms were in Japanese.

01:22:53.549 --> 01:22:55.363
- Yeah, the forms, they tell
you that you need to do that

01:22:55.363 --> 01:22:59.954
within two weeks of moving
here are also in Japanese.

01:22:59.954 --> 01:23:01.201
- It's simple, just learn Japanese

01:23:01.201 --> 01:23:02.479
in the two weeks that you're here.

01:23:02.479 --> 01:23:04.427
- The only reason we knew is
because the lawyers told us,

01:23:04.427 --> 01:23:05.660
"Hey, you've got do this."

01:23:05.660 --> 01:23:08.209
But if we didn't know
that, I don't know what,

01:23:08.209 --> 01:23:09.210
I would have just carried on living-

01:23:09.210 --> 01:23:11.738
- You need a dedicated
agency just to help you

01:23:11.738 --> 01:23:13.179
with all the admin stuff-

01:23:13.179 --> 01:23:14.709
- I mean, I can understand the language

01:23:14.709 --> 01:23:18.270
and I still have to learn
from my cousins who live here,

01:23:18.270 --> 01:23:20.234
like this is just how it works.

01:23:20.234 --> 01:23:21.067
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:23:21.067 --> 01:23:22.455
- Like oh shit, I have
to go to the town hall

01:23:22.455 --> 01:23:24.893
and register for my address

01:23:24.893 --> 01:23:28.022
and my health certificate
and all of that shit.

01:23:28.022 --> 01:23:30.408
I never had to experience
that living in Australia.

01:23:30.408 --> 01:23:32.713
I never had to experience that
while visiting here, right?

01:23:32.713 --> 01:23:35.099
So it's just, it's overwhelming.

01:23:35.099 --> 01:23:37.267
And like it's like massive kudos

01:23:37.267 --> 01:23:38.970
to people who don't know Japanese

01:23:38.970 --> 01:23:40.422
or even don't know English.

01:23:40.422 --> 01:23:42.358
gain, I don't know how the fuck they do it

01:23:42.358 --> 01:23:43.577
without the help of an agency.

01:23:43.577 --> 01:23:45.576
- To clarify, you can live here

01:23:45.576 --> 01:23:47.828
if you don't speak any Japanese
or for if you're learning.

01:23:47.828 --> 01:23:50.821
But I think if you're
somehow coming here alone

01:23:50.821 --> 01:23:54.174
without anyone helping you,
it's gonna be hell on earth.

01:23:54.174 --> 01:23:55.669
'Cause it was hell enough

01:23:55.669 --> 01:23:58.639
with multiple ways of
us having help, right?

01:23:58.639 --> 01:24:00.780
And I felt so bad for Joey,

01:24:00.780 --> 01:24:02.446
the amount of times I
have to ask him for help.

01:24:02.446 --> 01:24:04.341
I was like, he fucking
hates me at this point.

01:24:04.341 --> 01:24:05.174
- It's okay.

01:24:05.174 --> 01:24:06.607
- Every day I'm coming over with a form.

01:24:06.607 --> 01:24:07.571
- I still like you, don't worry.

01:24:07.571 --> 01:24:08.651
(guys laughing)

01:24:08.651 --> 01:24:09.550
- Like hey Joey, what does this say?

01:24:09.550 --> 01:24:12.221
And then also until you
figure this out, right?

01:24:12.221 --> 01:24:14.101
If you miss a package in the post,

01:24:14.101 --> 01:24:16.380
you get a little form through your mailbox

01:24:16.380 --> 01:24:18.992
that's all in Japanese
and you need to figure out

01:24:18.992 --> 01:24:20.989
how the fuck you're gonna
reschedule this thing.

01:24:20.989 --> 01:24:23.105
Luckily, I found a way eventually

01:24:23.105 --> 01:24:26.418
which was scan the barcode
with whatever thing you have,

01:24:26.418 --> 01:24:27.527
it'll take you to a website,

01:24:27.527 --> 01:24:29.687
use Google translate to translate it

01:24:29.687 --> 01:24:32.036
and then hope that the
translation are rough enough

01:24:32.036 --> 01:24:33.915
where you can like figure
out what's being said

01:24:33.915 --> 01:24:35.220
and that's what I do every time now.

01:24:35.220 --> 01:24:37.172
But for the first week
where I didn't know that,

01:24:37.172 --> 01:24:38.693
every time I missed a package,

01:24:38.693 --> 01:24:40.952
I was like, "Hey Joey,
can you call them up

01:24:40.952 --> 01:24:43.146
and tell them I'm gonna be home by 12?"

01:24:43.146 --> 01:24:46.507
- There was like a month where
I was calling up these guys

01:24:46.507 --> 01:24:49.517
more often for his packages
than it was for my own packages.

01:24:49.517 --> 01:24:51.976
- I felt so bad, but I was
like I need the package.

01:24:51.976 --> 01:24:53.246
It's my fucking desk.

01:24:53.246 --> 01:24:57.081
And again, okay, let's
trace it back again.

01:24:57.081 --> 01:25:01.106
